"""Triton implementation of aten::_convolution_double_backward.

Semantics (cross-correlation convention, tau = ``transposed``):

  tau=False:  O[n,co,z] = sum_{ci,k} X[n,ci, z*s-p+k*d] * W[co,ci,k]
  tau=True :  O[n,co,z] = sum_{ci,k} X[n,ci,i] * W[ci,co,k],  z = i*s-p+k*d

  grad_ggO    = op_tau(ggI, W) + op_tau(X, ggW) + ggb[co]
  grad_self   = op_{not tau}(gO, ggW)
  grad_weight[a,b,k] = sum_{n,q} G[n,a,q] * Xd[n,b, q*s-p+k*d]
                       (G, Xd) = (gO, ggI) if not tau else (ggI, gO)

All convolutions are gathered programmatically; every accumulation is fp32.

The reduction axis of every gather is the channel axis.  NCHW puts that axis
D*H*W apart while it is the innermost tile axis, so device kernels first
materialise channel-last (DHWC) copies of the activation operands and
kernel-position-major [k, C_in, C_out] copies of the weights (the weight's
dim0 is C_out when transposed=False and C_in when transposed=True).  All kernel
math, tile sizes, the autotune list and the fp32 accumulation order are
unchanged.
"""

